From 13bec6f800d66d3415bbf5e8077326c4b78ac53a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steve Brown <scbrown3@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 23:20:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] adapters: add quipu community evidence regime

quipu (github.com/scbrown/quipu) is a governed bitemporal
knowledge-graph store whose write gate emits three evidence planes per
decision: a writer-side guard trace, a signed verdict ledger fact with
the write's attribution sealed inside the evidence hash, and a
bitemporal policy snapshot (claim as-of vs now, authority grants).

Adds the native adapter with content-derived property categories and a
regime-internal source validator (field completeness, evidence-hash
recomputation, executor-chain consistency, grant scope); a native
fixture exported from quipu's seeded census benchmark with the
missing-policy degradation applied; smoke-corpus coverage (case,
paired annotations, scorer output); and adapter tests including one
showing a swapped attributed writer fails hash recomputation.

Registered in NATIVE_ADAPTERS only: REGIME_IDS remains the deposited
eight-regime manuscript contract, so the 64-case corpus arithmetic,
draft generation, and published results are unchanged; promoting the
regime is left as a corpus-version decision. Smoke-corpus count
assertions grow 8 -> 9 (64 -> 72 property rows) accordingly.
checksums.txt is refreshed, which also repairs the two rows
(pyproject.toml, __init__.py) that were stale at HEAD.

Co-authored-by: Claude (Anthropic) <noreply@anthropic.com>
